WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.921
<i>♪ It seems today that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.922 --> 00:08.174
<i>♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪</i>

00:08.175 --> 00:11.928
<i>♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.929 --> 00:14.847
<i>♪ On which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.848 --> 00:18.142
<i>♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.143 --> 00:21.604
<i>♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.605 --> 00:23.189
<i>♪ All the things that make us ♪</i>

00:23.190 --> 00:25.024
<i>♪ Laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:25.025 --> 00:30.155
<i>♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy. ♪</i>

00:34.910 --> 00:37.245
We now return to A Quiet Place,

00:37.246 --> 00:38.997
<i>starring a Jewish family.</i>

00:44.670 --> 00:47.171
<i>I'm finally all caught up on New Girl,</i>

00:47.172 --> 00:49.007
if you guys want to talk about that.

00:57.516 --> 00:59.475
I don't think they're going for it.

00:59.476 --> 01:00.727
Wait.

01:04.815 --> 01:06.065
I kind of like that Schmidt.

01:06.066 --> 01:08.317
You kind of like that Schmidt.

01:08.318 --> 01:10.403
All right, fellas, I got to get going.

01:10.404 --> 01:12.571
Aw, come on.
I want to get one more beer.

01:12.572 --> 01:14.407
Again! Again, again!

01:14.408 --> 01:16.492
Sorry, Peter, I got
to work early in the morning.

01:16.493 --> 01:18.202
Yeah, I'm out, too.

01:18.203 --> 01:19.495
Aw, crap, I don't have any cash.

01:19.496 --> 01:21.582
Hey, can one of you guys spot me?

01:21.583 --> 01:23.499
- Just put it on your card.
- I can't.

01:23.500 --> 01:25.918
Lois'll see the charge.
She thinks I'm still at work.

01:25.919 --> 01:26.919
Wa-peesh.

01:26.920 --> 01:28.337
Wha-What is that? What do you mean?

01:28.338 --> 01:29.922
What do you mean, like "Wha-pshh"?

01:29.923 --> 01:32.425
- Like that? Like a whip sound?
- Yeah. How did I do it?

01:32.426 --> 01:33.884
Very incorrectly.

01:33.885 --> 01:35.428
You don't have your own card,

01:35.429 --> 01:37.013
one that Lois doesn't know about?

01:37.014 --> 01:38.514
No. Lois would kill me.

01:38.515 --> 01:40.933
Ooh, what?-what?-what?-peesh.

01:40.934 --> 01:43.060
Indiana James?

01:43.061 --> 01:44.521
Anyone?

01:47.899 --> 01:52.385
456 Maple Drive, Suite 305.

01:52.386 --> 01:54.231
The "suite" is just a mailbox.

01:54.232 --> 01:56.532
This is where I get
all my credit card bills sent to

01:56.533 --> 01:59.160
and any other mail
Donna would be mad about.

01:59.161 --> 02:01.203
- Like what?
- Knives with gemstones,

02:01.204 --> 02:02.955
fat-butt magazines,

02:02.956 --> 02:05.786
whatever you think Ice-T
would keep in a nightstand.

02:05.787 --> 02:07.962
But really it's
for the credit card bills.

02:07.963 --> 02:09.711
I get some of my stuff here, too.

02:09.712 --> 02:12.251
Bills, catheters, residual checks.

02:12.252 --> 02:14.385
<i>- What are the checks for?
- Mostly Seinfeld.</i>

02:14.386 --> 02:16.802
<i>- You were on Seinfeld?
- Yeah, that's right.</i>

02:16.803 --> 02:19.555
Peter, I'm telling you, get
yourself a secret credit card.

02:19.556 --> 02:22.640
- You'll save yourself a lot of stress.
- Thanks, Cleveland.

02:22.641 --> 02:24.831
Ah, this is gonna make my life
so much better.

02:24.832 --> 02:27.146
Like when I used to make
fart balloon animals.

02:27.147 --> 02:28.898
All right. Who's next?

02:28.899 --> 02:32.234
- Can you make me a giraffe?
- Comin' right up.

02:39.451 --> 02:40.576
There you go.

02:40.577 --> 02:42.453
Don't pop that. You'll throw up.

02:42.454 --> 02:44.747
Oh, where did you find him?

02:44.748 --> 02:46.249
<i>He found me.</i>

02:50.337 --> 02:52.307
Hey, look who it is.

02:52.308 --> 02:53.923
You need us to pay
for your drinks again?

02:53.924 --> 02:56.133
No way. Guys, you are looking

02:56.134 --> 02:58.552
at the owner of his own credit card.

02:58.553 --> 03:00.262
All right. Good for you, Peter.

03:00.263 --> 03:01.597
You gonna pay us back?

03:01.598 --> 03:03.015
Come on, Joe, I don't interrupt you.

03:03.016 --> 03:05.851
Anyway, they even want me to do
one of Tina Fey's

03:05.852 --> 03:08.729
"look how quirky and busy
I am" credit card commercials.

03:08.730 --> 03:10.314
- Wow, really?
- Yeah.

03:10.315 --> 03:12.274
Oh, wait. I think it's starting.

03:12.275 --> 03:14.944
I hear a piano shuffle
and a clarinet. Taxi!

03:16.489 --> 03:19.365
- Where to?
- Any pet shop that sells snakes.

03:19.366 --> 03:21.325
Somebody puke in here?

03:21.326 --> 03:23.119
Yeah. Last night some guy...

03:23.120 --> 03:24.620
Hey! It's you!

03:24.621 --> 03:26.038
Gotta go.

03:27.541 --> 03:28.890
Hi. Can I help you?

03:28.891 --> 03:30.793
Can I press the button
that moves the clothes?

03:30.794 --> 03:33.255
Sir, that's reserved
for dry cleaners only.

03:36.883 --> 03:39.343
It's like a roller coaster ride
for pants.

03:39.344 --> 03:41.178
- Any calls?
- Your mistress called.

03:41.179 --> 03:43.097
She said she's waiting
at the hotel for you.

03:43.098 --> 03:44.557
Tell her I'll be there as soon as I can.

03:44.558 --> 03:46.560
She said she's pregnant.

03:46.561 --> 03:49.311
Do you know if that Mexican
doctor takes credit cards?

03:49.312 --> 03:51.021
He does.

03:52.649 --> 03:54.900
<i>If you're scummy and on the go,</i>

03:54.901 --> 03:57.528
<i>try the new Visa Gold Card.</i>

03:57.529 --> 04:00.823
<i>It's everywhere you want to be.</i>

04:05.577 --> 04:07.705
Hey, Dad, what do you got there?

04:07.706 --> 04:09.832
Chris, I got us lobsters for dinner.

04:09.833 --> 04:11.083
Cool.

04:11.084 --> 04:13.002
<i>Can... can I kill 'em?</i>

04:13.003 --> 04:14.670
Hmm, let me think.

04:14.671 --> 04:16.839
Of course you can kill 'em, sport.

04:16.840 --> 04:19.342
- Yay!
- Let's boil up some water.

04:28.518 --> 04:30.186
Package for Peter Griffin.

04:30.187 --> 04:31.770
Ah. I didn't order anything.

04:31.771 --> 04:34.106
<i>I-I mean, I could have if I wanted to.</i>

04:34.107 --> 04:36.066
I have a credit card.

04:36.067 --> 04:39.321
All right. Lot of cool people
on this route.

04:43.241 --> 04:44.450
Aah!

04:44.451 --> 04:46.744
Stop! You're hurting him.

04:46.745 --> 04:49.640
No, that's just air escaping.
They can't feel anything.

04:53.168 --> 04:55.878
- Hi. Can I help you?
- Yes. I'd like one of those flashlights

04:55.879 --> 04:57.337
with a vagina in it, please?

05:02.052 --> 05:03.174
Oh, no.

05:03.175 --> 05:04.637
O-Okay, okay, don't panic, everyone.

05:07.057 --> 05:09.389
Oh, he got you, Mom.

05:09.390 --> 05:12.144
I'm surprised this thing
still works after the day we had.

05:12.145 --> 05:14.227
- Meaning I had sex with...
- I know.

05:14.228 --> 05:15.351
- We get it.
- Ew.

05:15.352 --> 05:16.565
Five minutes ago,

05:16.566 --> 05:20.028
I had that flashlight
under my chin to look scary.

05:24.074 --> 05:25.908
Peter, are you wearing a costume

05:25.909 --> 05:28.787
from<I> Star Trek VI: The
Undiscovered Country?

05:44.469 --> 05:46.053
Peter, give me the credit card.

05:46.054 --> 05:47.472
How'd you find out?

05:49.516 --> 05:51.433
The UPS guy from earlier?

05:51.434 --> 05:54.144
Sorry, Peter. New rule:
I... I have to report

05:54.145 --> 05:57.314
any adults bragging
about having a credit card.

05:57.315 --> 05:59.567
But... but you said I was cool.

05:59.568 --> 06:01.069
Did you even mean it?

06:02.611 --> 06:04.781
Did you even mean it?!

06:08.285 --> 06:09.702
You know what bothers me even more

06:09.703 --> 06:11.704
than all the money
you put on that credit card?

06:11.705 --> 06:13.622
- Bonnie's new car?
- Oh, I know. What, does she think

06:13.623 --> 06:15.124
she's a (BLEEP) teenager?

06:15.125 --> 06:17.543
Wait, no, no.
What's worse is finding out

06:17.544 --> 06:19.295
how much you lie to me.

06:19.296 --> 06:20.796
I found your account online.

06:20.797 --> 06:22.840
Monday night you said
you were working late,

06:22.841 --> 06:25.467
but there's a $62 charge at The Clam.

06:25.468 --> 06:28.846
So whoever stole my card
is still in town.

06:28.847 --> 06:30.993
You just gave me the card, dummy.

06:30.994 --> 06:32.349
You said you had to work last weekend,

06:32.350 --> 06:34.018
then you bought a T-shirt that says

06:34.019 --> 06:35.853
"Working weekends... Does not compute"

06:35.854 --> 06:37.521
with Johnny 5 on it.

06:37.522 --> 06:39.064
I wanted to wait, but...

06:39.065 --> 06:41.609
Happy Mother's Day.

06:41.610 --> 06:43.694
You're not gonna weasel
your way out of this.

06:43.695 --> 06:45.662
You want to act like a child, Peter?

06:45.663 --> 06:47.740
Then I'm gonna treat you like a child.

06:47.741 --> 06:48.824
You're grounded.

06:48.825 --> 06:50.159
On whose authority?

06:50.160 --> 06:51.453
General Chang.

07:00.879 --> 07:03.380
Hey, Peter. Lois still mad at you?

07:03.381 --> 07:05.841
Yeah, but she's acting like
everything's fine on Facebook

07:05.842 --> 07:07.594
so she can post pictures of food.

07:17.103 --> 07:18.562
I mean, I've done some stupid stuff,

07:18.563 --> 07:20.272
but she's never grounded me before.

07:20.273 --> 07:23.395
Well, you could just leave
the house if you want.

07:23.396 --> 07:24.536
You are an adult.

07:24.537 --> 07:26.195
Brian, husbands are not adults.

07:26.196 --> 07:28.155
They are people who pay for things

07:28.156 --> 07:29.615
but are still somehow burdens.

07:29.616 --> 07:32.201
Worst part about it,
I'm gonna miss my Sunday shift

07:32.202 --> 07:34.161
at Clappy's Birthday Restaurant.

07:34.162 --> 07:37.122
We heard someone has a birthday.

07:37.123 --> 07:38.624
H.

07:42.212 --> 07:43.380
A.

07:47.217 --> 07:48.385
P.

07:52.138 --> 07:53.306
P.

07:56.893 --> 07:58.061
T.

08:01.815 --> 08:02.898
E.

08:02.899 --> 08:04.734
Happy birthday, Charlotte.

08:06.152 --> 08:08.237
Excuse me. My table
is celebrating the birthday

08:08.238 --> 08:11.300
of deceased Hawaiian pop singer
Israel Kamakawiwo'ole.

08:12.325 --> 08:14.743
Well, that's why we
call it Clappy's. Let's go.

08:14.744 --> 08:16.079
H.

08:23.336 --> 08:24.962
<i>- Hello?
- Peter.</i>

08:24.963 --> 08:26.964
<i>Peter, you're not gonna believe
whose car just broke down</i>

08:26.965 --> 08:29.171
<i>on Spooner Street. Tom Brady!</i>

08:29.172 --> 08:30.926
<i>- What?!
- Yeah. He's throwing passes</i>

08:30.927 --> 08:33.262
<i>to anyone who's able to leave his house.</i>

08:33.263 --> 08:35.310
<i>Ah, he's throwing one to Joe.</i>

08:35.311 --> 08:37.266
<i>Oh, my God,
Joe just stood up for a second.</i>

08:37.267 --> 08:38.600
<i>He put that pass</i>

08:38.601 --> 08:40.602
<i>where only a walking person
could catch it.</i>

08:40.603 --> 08:43.689
<i>That's how good he is...
His pass made me walk!</i>

08:43.690 --> 08:45.190
<i>And here comes Gisele.</i>

08:45.191 --> 08:47.866
<i>She's giving out Tag Heuer watches.</i>

08:47.867 --> 08:51.426
Aw. Lois? Can I please go out
and play with Tom Brady?

08:51.427 --> 08:52.448
<i>She's out here.</i>

08:52.449 --> 08:55.659
<i>Tom Brady's taking us all
to see an Anne Hathaway movie.</i>

08:55.660 --> 08:57.494
Oh. Uh...

08:57.495 --> 08:59.539
Oh, no, I'm grounded.

09:05.754 --> 09:08.517
Hey, it's my old wedding Tucks...

09:08.518 --> 09:10.077
Medicated Pads.

09:10.078 --> 09:11.967
Boy, my butt sure was like a match

09:11.968 --> 09:14.136
that needed to be extinguished that day.

09:14.137 --> 09:16.013
Oh, what a day that was.

09:16.014 --> 09:19.930
All the Preparation... H
I used on my fiery ring.

09:19.931 --> 09:21.344
I got to escape.

09:21.345 --> 09:22.541
But how?

09:22.542 --> 09:24.878
<i>Wait a minute, you saw
Shawshank Redemption, Peter.</i>

09:24.879 --> 09:26.564
How did Brooks get out of there?

09:30.153 --> 09:31.487
Aah!

09:31.488 --> 09:34.156
- Hey, possum.
- It's actually o-possum.

09:34.157 --> 09:35.617
O, is it?

09:44.542 --> 09:45.709
What the hell?

09:45.710 --> 09:47.543
Aah. Peter, what are you doing?

09:47.544 --> 09:48.879
I got to get out of here, Brian.

09:48.880 --> 09:50.422
I'm going crazy
sitting around the house.

09:50.423 --> 09:51.982
So you're tunneling out?

09:51.983 --> 09:54.218
Lois is gonna be furious
if she finds out.

09:54.219 --> 09:56.887
That's why Lois isn't going to find out.

09:56.888 --> 09:58.347
Right, boy?

09:58.348 --> 10:01.225
- What are you talking about?
- I'm talking about you...

10:01.226 --> 10:03.727
not being... a bad boy.

10:03.728 --> 10:06.271
I'm-I'm not... I'm not a bad boy.

10:06.272 --> 10:08.524
Then do not say anything to Lois.

10:08.525 --> 10:09.858
You hear me? Bad.

10:09.859 --> 10:11.360
Bad dog.

10:11.361 --> 10:13.187
So, we understand each other?

10:13.188 --> 10:14.780
Yeah, I'll be good. Trust me.

10:14.781 --> 10:16.741
I saw what you did to that black belt.

10:18.451 --> 10:20.869
I don't care what color your belt is,

10:20.870 --> 10:23.038
you're a child
and I am stronger than you.

10:23.039 --> 10:25.374
Oh, boo yourself.

10:25.375 --> 10:27.709
Boo yourself. She was the one
strutting around Pizza Hut

10:27.710 --> 10:29.378
with that trophy.

10:29.379 --> 10:32.756
Yeah, who's the Girls' Regional
Youth Karate Champ now, Kelsey?

10:32.757 --> 10:33.966
Huh?

10:33.967 --> 10:36.302
Kelsey?

10:57.949 --> 10:59.575
All right, down in the tunnel.

10:59.576 --> 11:02.745
Time to way-too-easily make a torch.

11:06.833 --> 11:08.625
Look, our Internet connection.

11:08.626 --> 11:10.085
Mom!

11:10.086 --> 11:11.253
Never mind.

11:11.254 --> 11:12.963
Mom!

11:12.964 --> 11:14.423
Never mind.

11:14.424 --> 11:16.258
Donna!

11:16.259 --> 11:17.427
Bonnie!

11:19.262 --> 11:20.762
I'm not on the Internet.

11:20.763 --> 11:23.182
Some people in this neighborhood read.

11:26.978 --> 11:29.479
Anyway, it was a beautiful ceremony.

11:29.480 --> 11:32.149
We laid my Uncle Reggie to rest
with the respect

11:32.150 --> 11:33.942
that he deserved.

11:33.943 --> 11:35.193
Aah! Uncle Reggie!

11:35.194 --> 11:37.446
I'm sorry we stuffed you
in that Hefty Cinch Sak

11:37.447 --> 11:38.864
and pushed you in the pond.

11:38.865 --> 11:40.616
Relax, guys. It's just me.

11:40.617 --> 11:42.701
You dug a hole all the way
from your house?

11:42.702 --> 11:44.119
Pretty cool, huh?

11:44.120 --> 11:46.538
Yeah, but what if Lois
notices you're gone?

11:46.539 --> 11:47.874
Trust me, I got it covered.

11:49.459 --> 11:52.170
Peter, there's some salmon
on the stove if you're hungry.

11:53.546 --> 11:55.964
Well, it's what I made.

11:55.965 --> 11:57.633
So, you guys want to see the tunnel?

11:57.634 --> 11:59.155
- Frick yeah.
- Let's go!

11:59.156 --> 12:01.429
- Right behind you.
- How 'bout you, Jerome? You in?

12:03.454 --> 12:05.474
Okay, well, he's busy.

12:05.475 --> 12:07.565
Peter Griffin...

12:07.566 --> 12:09.853
You've been a busy boy.

12:09.854 --> 12:12.147
- What was that?
- Just a cool way to say something.

12:12.148 --> 12:13.815
It wasn't that cool.

12:13.816 --> 12:15.317
All right, it's pretty neat, Peter,

12:15.318 --> 12:16.652
but we should probably get out of here.

12:16.653 --> 12:17.986
Yeah, sure.

12:17.987 --> 12:20.030
Unless anyone wants to see a salamander.

12:20.031 --> 12:21.239
Oh, look at it.

12:21.240 --> 12:22.491
I named him Sally.

12:22.492 --> 12:24.158
Slippy-ass little bug right there.

12:24.159 --> 12:25.661
Okay, this is pretty cool.

12:25.662 --> 12:27.789
Come on, I'll show you the rest.

12:30.375 --> 12:31.583
Look at these handprints.

12:31.584 --> 12:33.710
Somebody did the perfect cartwheel.

12:33.711 --> 12:35.671
Actually, Peter, there's elbow prints

12:35.672 --> 12:37.547
and knee prints all around this thing.

12:37.548 --> 12:39.466
The perfect cartwheel.

12:39.467 --> 12:41.843
And there's scuffled dirt and
a little bit of blood over here.

12:41.844 --> 12:44.513
Perhaps the ancients
cartwheeled everywhere.

12:44.514 --> 12:46.932
Peter, did you trip on a root
and eat it big-time?

12:46.933 --> 12:48.350
No, I did not.

12:48.351 --> 12:50.686
Uh, hang on. There's a guy
tunneling the other way.

12:50.687 --> 12:52.570
Pretty cramped, huh?

12:52.571 --> 12:54.032
You said it.

12:54.033 --> 12:55.857
Next time, I pay for business class.

12:55.858 --> 12:57.526
Right?

12:57.527 --> 12:59.695
That guy was in the paper
for hitting his wife.

13:01.948 --> 13:05.701
Peter, are you sure this tunnel
is structurally sound?

13:05.702 --> 13:08.495
Don't worry, guys.
I'll cartwheel back for help.

13:08.496 --> 13:09.913
Aah!

13:09.914 --> 13:10.956
A root.

13:10.957 --> 13:12.749
I ate it big-time.

13:12.750 --> 13:14.752
Look out!

13:24.512 --> 13:25.804
Oh, my God.

13:25.805 --> 13:28.056
The tunnel's completely
collapsed on both sides.

13:28.057 --> 13:29.975
Oh, no. We're stuck down here.

13:29.976 --> 13:31.601
Hey, guys.

13:31.602 --> 13:33.515
Hey, look, it's the dumb beaver.

13:33.516 --> 13:35.731
- You live down here?
- Sure do.

13:35.732 --> 13:38.817
Welcome to my running-out-of-Airbnb.

13:39.986 --> 13:42.238
No, but this is very serious.

13:51.097 --> 13:53.246
Great. Peter, this is just great.

13:53.247 --> 13:56.189
Because you can't stand up
to your wife, I'm gonna die.

13:56.190 --> 13:58.335
Relax, Quagmire. Nobody's gonna die.

13:58.336 --> 14:00.929
What do you think happens
when we run out of air, genius?

14:00.930 --> 14:02.584
Air. Right.

14:02.585 --> 14:04.092
You know, I'd only taken
the other three elements

14:04.093 --> 14:05.177
into account.

14:05.178 --> 14:08.904
Earth, wind, fire, water.

14:08.905 --> 14:11.433
- Where's air?
- Wind is air.

14:11.434 --> 14:15.145
Who's that, Joey Swanson
or Bill Nye the Science Guy?

14:15.146 --> 14:16.646
Peter, can't you dig us out of here?

14:16.647 --> 14:18.315
No, I left my tools at The Clam.

14:18.316 --> 14:19.983
Uh, what's standard protocol

14:19.984 --> 14:21.443
for when the cops start looking for us?

14:21.444 --> 14:22.944
Uh, I'm not sure.

14:22.945 --> 14:25.447
I just give out stickers
if kids come to the station.

14:25.448 --> 14:26.990
I guess the only chance we have

14:26.991 --> 14:29.100
is if Brian sells me out to Lois.

14:29.101 --> 14:32.287
What I wouldn't give to be
with a woman just one more time.

14:32.288 --> 14:34.998
You can go over to that wall,
make yourself a dirt-gina.

14:34.999 --> 14:36.875
- This wall here?
- No, silly.

14:36.876 --> 14:38.376
That wall's a guy.

14:44.342 --> 14:46.343
We now return to Planet Earth,

14:46.344 --> 14:48.887
<i>with its original narrator,
who was let go.</i>

14:48.888 --> 14:51.290
<i>The Earth's oceans are very,</i>

14:51.291 --> 14:53.266
<i>uh... vast?</i>

14:53.267 --> 14:55.852
<i>And, uh, a lot of fish. Yeah.</i>

14:55.853 --> 14:57.145
<i>Couple of whales.</i>

14:57.146 --> 14:58.647
<i>Some flora and fauna.</i>

14:58.648 --> 15:02.234
<i>Both down there in the,
uh, uncharted depths?</i>

15:02.235 --> 15:05.071
<i>Wow, what are those? Sharks?</i>

15:07.490 --> 15:10.659
<i>We've, uh, probably got
a commercial break coming up.</i>

15:10.660 --> 15:12.744
<i>Uh... Oh. Oh, really?</i>

15:12.745 --> 15:14.621
<i>Four hours, no commercials?</i>

15:14.622 --> 15:17.249
<i>Wow, is that right?</i>

15:17.250 --> 15:19.626
<i>Some penguins over there.</i>

15:19.627 --> 15:21.628
Brian, have you seen Peter?

15:21.629 --> 15:23.595
N-No. Why?

15:23.596 --> 15:25.570
Well, I haven't seen him all morning.

15:25.571 --> 15:28.260
I'm worried he left the house
and got into some kind of trouble.

15:28.261 --> 15:30.846
He'll turn up. I'm sure he's fine.

15:30.847 --> 15:32.347
Phew.

15:32.348 --> 15:34.189
Somethin' on your mind there, bud?

15:34.190 --> 15:37.007
- I'm not a bad boy.
- Uh, nobody said you were.

15:37.008 --> 15:39.437
Good. Because I'm not a bad boy.
I'm a good boy.

15:39.438 --> 15:42.107
<i>How would you like to be
a very good boy?</i>

15:42.108 --> 15:44.169
- Tell me how. Tell me how.
- Where's the fat man?

15:44.170 --> 15:46.714
- Aw, damn it.
- But I promised Peter.

15:46.715 --> 15:48.196
What is it? What is it, boy?

15:50.867 --> 15:53.201
The fat man dug a tunnel to go hang out

15:53.202 --> 15:54.703
with Cleveland, Joe and Quagmire?

15:54.704 --> 15:56.204
We've got to tell someone.

15:56.205 --> 15:57.372
What is it, Stewie?

15:59.978 --> 16:01.710
Daddy went to a Peter Cetera concert

16:01.711 --> 16:04.171
in Cleveland with Robin Tunney?

16:04.172 --> 16:05.922
<i>Robin Tunney from The Mentalist slept</i>

16:05.923 --> 16:08.259
with the entire Cleveland Browns team?

16:08.260 --> 16:12.637
<i>Bad Moms 1 and 2 are available
on most streaming platforms?</i>

16:12.638 --> 16:14.222
Don't-don't do that, Mila.

16:14.223 --> 16:16.225
Not-not on this show.

16:18.813 --> 16:20.812
<i>Good afternoon. I'm Tom Tucker,
here with a story</i>

16:20.813 --> 16:23.507
<i>that's "anchor out
of the studio" important.</i>

16:23.508 --> 16:25.817
<i>Rescue attempts are underway
to free four men</i>

16:25.818 --> 16:28.498
<i>who have been trapped
in an underground tunnel.</i>

16:28.499 --> 16:31.181
<i>One of the men
is Quahog's own Peter Griffin.</i>

16:31.182 --> 16:33.857
<i>Channel 5 reached out
to his family for comment.</i>

16:33.858 --> 16:35.243
<i>Here's what they had to say.</i>

16:35.244 --> 16:38.240
<i>I'm about to take my laptop
into the bathroom.</i>

16:38.241 --> 16:40.457
<i>I ask that you please respect my privacy</i>

16:40.458 --> 16:41.974
<i>in this difficult time.</i>

16:41.975 --> 16:43.085
<i>Thank you.</i>

16:44.227 --> 16:46.213
Anyone else having trouble breathing?

16:46.214 --> 16:47.505
Could just be allergies.

16:47.506 --> 16:49.238
Yeah. Yeah, you think it's allergies?

16:49.239 --> 16:51.009
You don't think it's because
we're running out of air?

16:51.010 --> 16:52.260
It's hard to say.

16:52.261 --> 16:54.179
I don't know
how severe your allergies are.

16:54.180 --> 16:55.680
- Different people are allergic...
- You are such a moron.

16:55.681 --> 16:57.682
- You know, I hope we do die down here.
- Oh, that's nice.

16:57.683 --> 16:59.351
- So I never have to listen...
- That's a nice thing

16:59.352 --> 17:00.518
to say to a lifelong friend.

17:00.519 --> 17:02.020
Ah. Ah.

17:02.021 --> 17:03.271
I'm gonna kill you, Peter!

17:03.272 --> 17:04.940
All right, calm down.

17:04.941 --> 17:07.526
Let's not use the rest of
our oxygen to kill each other.

17:08.694 --> 17:10.677
So if we're all gonna die anyway,

17:10.678 --> 17:13.057
what's the worst thing
you guys have ever done?

17:14.081 --> 17:15.659
Okay, I'll go first.

17:15.660 --> 17:16.952
Lois...

17:16.953 --> 17:18.636
once killed a woman.

17:18.637 --> 17:20.163
Seems like a secret about Lois.

17:20.164 --> 17:22.624
<i>Yeah. But I picked out the woman.</i>

17:22.625 --> 17:26.127
Well, I, uh... I, uh, went
to a Coldplay concert by myself.

17:26.128 --> 17:27.712
What? That's terrible.

17:27.713 --> 17:29.937
- Why would you do that?
- I like Coldplay!

17:29.938 --> 17:31.800
They were playing in Boston,
so I made the trip.

17:31.801 --> 17:34.177
Great show, I got to say. Very visual.

17:34.178 --> 17:36.471
<i>It was visual. I was at that show, too.</i>

17:36.472 --> 17:38.348
What? You were there?

17:38.349 --> 17:39.724
No, I'm just kidding.

17:40.977 --> 17:43.019
Uh, I like Lil Yachty, man.

17:43.020 --> 17:44.813
I don't know nothin' about that mess.

17:44.814 --> 17:46.398
<i>But I did go to that show.</i>

17:46.399 --> 17:47.732
<i>Didn't mean to.</i>

17:47.733 --> 17:49.484
<i>I said "Kid 'n Play" on the phone,</i>

17:49.485 --> 17:52.237
<i>but they didn't understand me,
so I got Coldplay.</i>

17:52.238 --> 17:54.698
<i>One other time I said "Kid 'n Play"</i>

17:54.699 --> 17:57.160
<i>and I got Cirque du Soleil.</i>

17:57.161 --> 18:01.038
<i>I'm thinking maybe Kid 'n Play
doesn't perform anymore.</i>

18:03.374 --> 18:05.250
What's that sound?

18:05.251 --> 18:07.085
Probably just the movie
in the next theater.

18:07.086 --> 18:09.755
I hope the rest of the tunnel
isn't about to collapse.

18:13.092 --> 18:16.408
<i>Hello? This is the Quahog
Emergency Rescue Team.</i>

18:16.409 --> 18:17.993
<i>We're gonna get you out of there.</i>

18:17.994 --> 18:19.222
- Oh, fresh air!
- Oh, my God!

18:19.223 --> 18:20.557
- Oh, my God!
- Oh, we're saved!

18:20.558 --> 18:22.965
<i>So, uh, full disclosure,</i>

18:22.966 --> 18:25.353
<i>the last time I did this,
the guy got torn in half.</i>

18:25.354 --> 18:28.239
<i>Probably won't happen again,
but they want me to say it.</i>

18:28.240 --> 18:29.434
We're saved.

18:29.435 --> 18:31.798
<i>- Probably saved.
- I told them.</i>

18:31.799 --> 18:32.906
All right, whatever we do,

18:32.907 --> 18:34.779
we're not gonna talk
about kissing practice.

18:34.780 --> 18:36.946
- Totally. - No way.
- Oh, no, I wouldn't.

18:36.947 --> 18:38.487
<i>You guys ready to come up?</i>

18:38.488 --> 18:41.286
We've been doing kissing
practice and I'm the best at it.

18:53.299 --> 18:55.150
Yay. The cop.

18:55.151 --> 18:56.426
Okay.

18:58.179 --> 19:00.058
<i>Stop. Stop. I'm stuck.</i>

19:00.059 --> 19:02.199
You're slightly too big for the hole.

19:02.200 --> 19:04.976
Can you take off your shirt
and come up in just pants?

19:04.977 --> 19:08.274
<i>Is Rebecca the cashier
from Rite Aid there?</i>

19:08.275 --> 19:09.499
She is.

19:09.500 --> 19:11.316
<i>Can you have her turn around?</i>

19:14.570 --> 19:16.056
Gross.

19:16.057 --> 19:17.489
Oh, that's not Rebecca. That's Gretchen.

19:17.490 --> 19:18.573
That's fine.

19:18.574 --> 19:20.241
Peter?

19:20.242 --> 19:22.494
<i>- Oh, Lois.
- ♪ I just want ♪</i>

19:22.495 --> 19:25.121
<i>♪ To be the one you run to ♪</i>

19:25.122 --> 19:27.791
<i>♪ I just want to be the one
you come to ♪</i>

19:27.792 --> 19:29.459
<i>♪ I just want... ♪</i>

19:29.460 --> 19:32.003
What the hell were you thinking?!

19:32.004 --> 19:34.005
Peter, the whole reason
you were grounded

19:34.006 --> 19:35.924
was because you were lying to me.

19:35.925 --> 19:38.635
And then you lied to me
about the tunnel.

19:38.636 --> 19:41.429
Look, I-I'm sorry I lied to you.

19:41.430 --> 19:43.848
I'm sorry I lied about the credit card.

19:43.849 --> 19:46.494
And I'm sorry I lied about the tunnel.

19:46.495 --> 19:48.242
I know I was acting stupid,

19:48.243 --> 19:49.896
and I deserved to be grounded.

19:49.897 --> 19:52.837
Peter, I don't want
to have to ground you.

19:52.838 --> 19:53.842
You're my husband.

19:53.843 --> 19:56.319
I just don't want you to lie to me.

19:56.320 --> 19:58.756
I lie to you
'cause you treat me like a kid.

19:58.757 --> 20:01.324
Act like a man and I'll
stop treating you like a kid.

20:01.325 --> 20:03.538
Look like a kid,
I'll start acting like a man.

20:03.539 --> 20:04.661
- What?
- I'm sorry, Lois.

20:04.662 --> 20:06.329
That's just the tunnel talkin'.

20:06.330 --> 20:08.415
So, Chris, you happy
to have your dad back?

20:08.416 --> 20:10.625
Yeah, you know what, Tom,
I think we're all gonna go home

20:10.626 --> 20:13.539
and charge our laptops
a little longer tonight.

20:13.540 --> 20:15.296
You just never know when
you're gonna run out of juice

20:15.297 --> 20:17.186
and have to use your phone.

20:17.187 --> 20:19.384
You know, just because we're reporters

20:19.385 --> 20:22.066
doesn't mean we're devoid of emotion.

20:22.067 --> 20:24.187
Go on and head home with your family.

20:24.188 --> 20:25.306
Thanks, Tom.

20:25.307 --> 20:27.475
That's a...

20:27.476 --> 20:30.729
that's a very horny kid right there.

20:36.735 --> 20:38.862
Oh, it's so beautiful here.

20:38.863 --> 20:41.156
Nothing but the best
for my beautiful bride

20:41.157 --> 20:42.407
on her honeymoon.

20:42.408 --> 20:44.325
I'm sorry, sir, the chef said

20:44.326 --> 20:46.923
he can't make
a chocolate chip gumball pizza.

20:46.924 --> 20:49.007
Oh, that's okay. It's not your fault.

20:49.008 --> 20:51.332
I'll just need another minute then.

20:51.333 --> 20:53.835
Her.

20:53.836 --> 20:55.503
I'm on it.

20:55.504 --> 20:57.505
I love you so much.

20:57.506 --> 20:59.592
Mwah.